    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t78r5k8",
      "content": "Pathology is the study of diseases, their causes, mechanisms, structural changes, and functional consequences. In nursing competitive examinations such as RRB Nursing, pathology questions commonly come from cell injury, inflammation, degeneration, tumors, blood disorders, and immune disorders. Understanding pathology helps nurses recognize disease processes and provide appropriate patient care."
    },
